Use a constant offsetof() argument in PEImageReader

offsetof() with a non-constant array subscript is a Microsoft extension.
GCC rejects it with "'index' is not a constant expression", which breaks
the mingw-w64 cross build. Compute the data directory entry offset from
the array base instead, which is equivalent and standard C++.

Upstream (getsentry/crashpad) only builds this file with MSVC and clang-cl.

--- a/snapshot/win/pe_image_reader.cc
+++ b/snapshot/win/pe_image_reader.cc
@@ -424,9 +424,12 @@ bool PEImageReader::ImageDataDirectoryEntryT(
     return false;
   }

+  // offsetof() with a non-constant array subscript is a Microsoft extension:
+  // GCC requires a constant expression, so compute the entry offset by hand.
   if (nt_headers.FileHeader.SizeOfOptionalHeader <
-          offsetof(decltype(nt_headers.OptionalHeader), DataDirectory[index]) +
-              sizeof(nt_headers.OptionalHeader.DataDirectory[index]) ||
+          offsetof(decltype(nt_headers.OptionalHeader), DataDirectory) +
+              (index + 1) *
+                  sizeof(nt_headers.OptionalHeader.DataDirectory[0]) ||
       nt_headers.OptionalHeader.NumberOfRvaAndSizes <= index) {
     return false;
   }
